    ["——在那个平行世界里，奥黛丽和苏茜合作解决了佛尔思同伴的案件。\n\n      贝克兰德，霍尔家的花园。奥黛丽坐在吊椅上，阳光透过藤蔓洒下斑驳的光影。\n      几天前，佛尔思·沃尔来访时的神情又浮现在她眼前。那位气质慵懒的作家露出郑重的神色：“我有位同伴被关入了监狱，正等待着最后的审判，我希望你们能够救她出来，无论用什么办法。”\n      而同行的格莱林特子爵派人咨询了熟悉的大律师，对方说有把握只是轻判，但无罪辩护的难度很高，除非当事人能拿到精神有问题或者心智发育不健全的医疗证明……\n      奥黛丽记得自己当时答应了佛尔思会认真考虑。作家小姐离开时还回头看了一眼，淡蓝色的眼睛里藏着期待。\n      “医疗证明……”奥黛丽轻声自语，眉头微蹙。她不是没想过用霍尔家的影响力去疏通，但那会暴露她和佛尔思、休之间的关系。况且，那位黑帮头目虽然出具了原谅声明，严重伤害的案件却依然可能被起诉。\n      身旁趴着的苏茜竖起耳朵，用只有奥黛丽能听见的声音小声说：“那个黑帮头目，还在医院里？”\n      奥黛丽低头看她，目光微动。\n      “我去试一试。”苏茜摇了摇尾巴提议道。\n      当天夜里，苏茜悄悄潜入病房。她用“观众”的能力温和地引导那位“体面的绅士”回忆——对方终于记起，是自己先动了手，休只是自卫。醒来后，他主动向检察官更正了证词。\n      几天后，休被无罪释放。佛尔思来霍尔家道谢时，感慨“检察官突然发现了新证据，运气真好”。\n      奥黛丽微笑着点头：“是啊，运气真好。”\n      苏茜趴在她脚边，尾巴拍打着地毯，心满意足。"] = "—In that parallel world, Audrey and Susie worked together to solve the case involving Fors's companion. \n\n      Бэкланд, the Hall family garden. Audrey sat on a hanging chair, sunlight casting dappled light and shadows through the vines. \n      A few days ago, the expression on Fors Wall's face when she visited appeared in her mind again. That lazy-tempered writer had shown a solemn look: \"I have a companion who has been thrown into prison and is waiting for the final verdict. I hope you can save her, no matter what method you use.\" \n      And the accompanying Viscount Glaint had sent someone to consult a well-known lawyer, who said there was a chance for a light sentence, but an acquittal was very difficult unless the defendant could obtain a medical certificate stating they had mental issues or were mentally underdeveloped... \n      Audrey remembered that she had promised Fors she would consider it carefully. When the writer left, she had looked back, anticipation hidden in her light blue eyes. \n      \"Medical certificate...\" Audrey whispered to herself, her brows slightly furrowed. It wasn't that she hadn't thought about using the Hall family's influence to pull strings, but that would expose her relationship with Fors and Xio. Moreover, although the gang leader had issued a statement of forgiveness, the case of grievous injury could still be prosecuted. \n      Susie, lying beside her, pricked up her ears and whispered in a voice only Audrey could hear: \"That gang leader, is he still in the hospital?\" \n      Audrey looked down at her, her gaze flickering. \n      \"I'll go give it a try,\" Susie suggested, wagging her tail. \n      That night, Susie quietly snuck into the hospital room. She used her Зритель ability to gently guide the \"decent gentleman\" to recall—the other party finally remembered that he had struck first and that Xio was only acting in self-defense. After waking up, he took the initiative to correct his testimony to the prosecutor. \n      A few days later, Xio was acquitted. When Fors came to the Hall residence to thank her, she sighed, \"The prosecutor suddenly found new evidence; what good luck.\" \n      Audrey smiled and nodded: \"Yes, what good luck.\" \n      Susie lay at her feet, her tail thumping against the carpet, feeling satisfied.",
